  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened Local Civil Society Organizations for Responsive and Accountable Governance in Human Rights and Gender Equality in Timor-Leste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This action directly supports the EU&#xbf;s objective of strengthening civil society organizations (CSOs) as independent, participatory, and empowered actors of good governance and development, with a particular focus on gender equality and youth empowerment&#xbf;core themes in EU external action policy and this Call for Proposals (CfP 183137). &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It addresses the specific objective of enhancing the leadership, governance, and advocacy capacity of local CSOs in Timor-Leste to effectively engage in policy dialogue, promote democratic participation and human rights, and advance inclusive and sustainable development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposed action responds to these interlinked challenges through an integrated, multi-level strategy that strengthens:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;The advocacy capacity and leadership of CSOs to engage in evidence-based dialogue with government institutions at national and municipal levels;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;The institutional and financial sustainability of CSOs through tailored capacity-building, digital and operational support, and fundraising strategies;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;The empowerment of women, youth, and GBV survivors as active rights-holders and agents of change within their communities and civic spaces.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;This action builds on and complements existing national frameworks and commitments, including:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;The Government of Timor-Leste&#xbf;s National Action Plan on Gender-Based Violence (PAN GBV) and obligations under CEDAW and the Universal Periodic Review (UPR);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;Ongoing EU and donor-supported programs that promote civic engagement, gender equality, social inclusion, and democratic governance. The Action strategically aligns with initiatives like the EU-funded Spotlight Initiative, ensuring complementarity and avoiding any overlap. It also reinforces the commitments outlined in the EU Gender Action Plan III (2021&#xbf;2025), particularly regarding the empowerment of women and girls, and is fully consistent with the EU Youth Action Plan, promoting youth civic engagement, leadership, and rights-based participation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;The platforms and reach of key national actors&#xbf;FONGTIL, Asosiasaun HAK, and FOKUPERS&#xbf;who bring deep local legitimacy and longstanding leadership in advocacy, civic education, and service delivery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;By concentrating implementation in &lt;strong&gt;Dili, Baucau, Ermera, Aileu and Oecusse&lt;/strong&gt;, while maintaining strong national-level coordination, the action ensures&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;both depth and breadth&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;of impact. Activities are also designed to avoid duplication by coordinating with existing CSO coalitions and network, aligning with state-led processes such as the General State Budget cycle, and leveraging ongoing media and public engagement tools such as Lafaek magazine, podcasts, and television talk shows.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
